    "# NaniGPT — Day 7: Voice journal (Gemma 4 audio)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Goal:** add the 4th distinct use of Gemma 4 — native audio understanding — to the Daily check-in tab. Caregiver speaks at 11pm, Gemma 4 transcribes, then dispatches the same tools as the text journal.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why two-stage** (transcribe → then act, not audio→tools in one call):\n",
    "1. Lets the caregiver verify what NaniGPT heard before anything is logged\n",
    "2. Failure of transcription is recoverable without dispatching wrong tool calls\n",
    "3. Reuses the validated text-journal pipeline\n",
    "4. Cleaner writeup story\n",
    "\n",
    "**Pre-req:** notebooks 01-03 already loaded in this Colab session.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1 — Helper: audio → transcript\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import torch\n",
    "\n",
    "TRANSCRIBE_SYSTEM = '''You are a transcription assistant. Output ONLY the words spoken in the audio — no commentary, no labels, no quotation marks. If the audio is silent or unintelligible, output exactly: [unintelligible]'''\n",
    "\n",
    "def transcribe_audio(audio_path):\n",
    "    if not audio_path:\n",
    "        return ''\n",
    "    messages = [\n",
    "        {'role': 'system', 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': TRANSCRIBE_SYSTEM}]},\n",
    "        {'role': 'user', 'content': [\n",
    "            {'type': 'audio', 'audio': audio_path},\n",
    "            {'type': 'text',  'text': 'Transcribe this caregiver journal entry. Output only the spoken words.'},\n",
    "        ]},\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "    inputs = tokenizer.apply_chat_template(\n",
    "        messages, add_generation_prompt=True, tokenize=True,\n",
    "        return_dict=True, return_tensors='pt',\n",
    "    ).to(model.device)\n",
    "    with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "        out = model.generate(**inputs, max_new_tokens=400, temperature=0.1, top_p=0.9, do_sample=False)\n",
    "    text = tokenizer.decode(out[0][inputs['input_ids'].shape[1]:], skip_special_tokens=True)\n",
    "    return text.strip()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2 — Quick test before wiring to UI\n",
    "\n",
    "Upload one of your voice recordings (`.m4a`, `.wav`, `.mp3` all work). Confirm the transcript looks reasonable.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from google.colab import files\n",
    "uploaded = files.upload()\n",
    "audio_filename = list(uploaded.keys())[0]\n",
    "print('Uploaded:', audio_filename)\n",
    "\n",
    "transcript = transcribe_audio(audio_filename)\n",
    "print('--- TRANSCRIPT ---')\n",
    "print(transcript)\n",
    "print('------------------')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3 — Voice handler that chains transcribe + agent\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def handle_voice_journal(audio_path):\n",
    "    if not audio_path:\n",
    "        return '', 'No audio recorded yet.', '', ''\n",
    "    transcript = transcribe_audio(audio_path)\n",
    "    if not transcript or transcript.lower().strip() in ('[unintelligible]', '(unintelligible)'):\n",
    "        return ('[unintelligible]',\n",
    "                \"⚠️ I couldn't make out what was said. Try recording again in a quieter spot.\",\n",
    "                '', '')\n",
    "    warm, calls_text, raw = run_journal(transcript)\n",
    "    # prepend a small note so the caregiver knows the transcript drove the actions\n",
    "    warm_with_attribution = f\"_From your voice note:_  \\n\\n{warm}\"\n",
    "    return transcript, warm_with_attribution, calls_text, raw"
   ]
  },
  {
